From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:33:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AROS: stop and join the MCP stdin thread when a session ends

Problem: the AROS stdin thread (0010) was detached and only noticed a
  finished session when it had a line to deliver. A session that ended
  without end of input (failed initialization, an overlong request) left it
  blocked in a read, and AROS's pthread exit handler waits for running
  threads: the process could not end. Supervisor review R2.
Rationale: the thread's JoinHandle is kept; serve_stdio stops and joins it
  (on a blocking thread) after serve_io returns. Where the handler answers
  WaitForChar (the console), the thread waits in 100 ms steps and notices
  the stop at once. The PIPE: handler does not answer WaitForChar and has no
  way to take back a pending read (one reader, one writer; a read ends only
  with data or the writer's close; workbench/fs/pipe), so there the join
  waits for the client to write or close, and stderr says so. The thread is
  never abandoned while its code could be unloaded. Upstream on POSIX hosts
  behaves the same (Tokio's stdin read keeps a failed-init process alive
  until the client closes stdin; checked on macOS).
Scope: cfg(target_os = "aros"); photocraft-aros-stdin gains c/stdin_wait.c.
Upstream-status: local-only.
Prerequisites: 0010, 0015.
Verification: guest cases with stdin held open after failed initialization
  and after an overlong request, then closed; console case not automated.
Removal: when AROS reads can be cancelled or Tokio's stdin works there.
